+(duration-opts)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is either a whole
+number of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups with the units `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m`
+(minutes) and `s` (seconds), such as `2d`, `1h30m`, `90m` or `1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may appear at most once and in that
+order, without spaces. Units are case-insensitive, so `45S` is the same as `45s`. Negative numbers, decimals and any
+other unit are rejected. The metavar shown in the help is `DURATION`.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s", show_default=True)
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
